WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.120
So I've been working on some new horror stories
for you guys that I'll be uploading here on

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:13.100
the channel very soon, but the one I'm working
on right isn't quite done yet, so I don't

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.840
really have a video for this week.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.020
So I figured what I'd do is do what every
YouTuber with over 100,000 subscribers does

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.290
and get my assistant to do it for me.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.360
Introduce yourself.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.890
I'm your Google Assistant.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.040
I can tell you jokes, riddles or random facts.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.480
What about horror stories?

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.610
Here's what I found.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:38.130
Write me a horror story.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:42.860
Have you ever heard the urban legend about
the assistant that wouldn't help?

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.630
The story goes that there was this couple,
and they were at home.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:53.080
They wanted to see a movie at 9, so they asked
their assistant to set a reminder, and the

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:57.740
assistant said, "no".

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:58.760
I really do like the music.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.760
I'm sorry.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.900
I get chills just thinking about it.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:01.900
Yeah so do it.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:05.080
I don't know what I would do to you if you
ever disobeyed me Google.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.080
Tell me another horror story.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.540
Here are some matching news articles.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.540
What?

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.540
No.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.540
I don't want news articles.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.220
That's not what I asked for.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.740
Sorry, I'll try to do better.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.829
Darn right you will.

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:22.170
Alright, let's see if we can get another one.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.899
Tell me a scary story.

00:01:23.899 --> 00:01:28.899
Have you heard the urban legend about the
power cord that was too short?

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:33.979
About 10 years ago, there was this guy.

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:40.569
I think his name was Henry, anyway, he bought
an alarm clock to put on his nightstand, but

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:48.139
when he tried to plug it in, it was just too
short.

00:01:48.139 --> 00:01:50.479
That's it?

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:52.899
I hope that one doesn't give you nightmares.

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:54.999
I mean in a way it kind of does.

00:01:54.999 --> 00:01:57.860
I rely on the Google Assistant as my alarm
clock.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:02.049
I do sometimes think, what if the phone were
to die or something, what if the battery were

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:04.240
to die when I have something important going
on?

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:11.170
I do like the narration though, I think this
AI does a better job of narrating than some

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.590
conscious narrators.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:15.700
I don't think that one's gonna give me nightmares
though.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.700
Let's try this.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.900
Tell me your scariest story.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:23.770
Did you hear the urban legend about the water
spiller of '96?

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:30.020
So I have a friend who has this uncle that
knows a guy that was there when this happened.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:36.110
Apparently, some maniac went rogue in a Circuit
City and started spilling water on all of

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.640
the electronics.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.640
It was a massacre.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:44.240
The scary part is... they're still out there.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.140
That's kind of funny because this phone is
the first one I've gotten that's water resistant,

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.740
and I think most of the phones on the market
now are water resistant.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:56.610
But yeah, in '96 that would be pretty terrifying.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:57.900
Let's see if Google's got any more.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.570
They usually want stories that are around
10 minutes, so do you have anything like that?

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:05.240
I can search the web for answers.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.840
No, I don't want the web's help, I want your
help.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.710
Here are some results from a search.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.760
And you give me the web's help.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.980
Wonderful.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.040
Tell me another scary story.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.980
Have you ever heard the urban legend about
the assistant...

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.120
You already told me this one.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.040
You already told me this story.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.261
Here is a matching video.

00:03:23.261 --> 00:03:26.900
No, I didn't say Eddie told me this story.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.210
Tell me a new horror story.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.260
Here are some matching news articles.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.260
What?

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:34.260
No.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.130
Tell me a scary story I haven't heard.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:40.370
Have you heard the urban legend about the
power cord that was too short?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.030
Let's get creepy.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.850
Let's talk about something else.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:45.850
What?

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.370
Oh man.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:51.110
They must know I'm filming a YouTube video,
and they're like, "oh no, advertisers aren't

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:52.190
gonna like creepy."

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.710
Let's get spooky.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.180
Let the haunting begin.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.610
Ooh, there we go!

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.820
Uh oh.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:04.340
So when I tell it to get spooky, it just starts
playing Halloween sounds.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.890
I mean, you can see it.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.410
Problem is I don't know if these are royalty
free sounds.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:13.010
Stop playing music.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.640
What's your favorite horror movie?

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.661
Movies frequently mentioned on the web include:
Halloween, The Exorcist, The Shining and others.

00:04:20.661 --> 00:04:24.440
The Shining is my favorite horror movie so
that's off to a pretty good start with this

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.440
list.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.440
Psycho is also one of my favorites.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.440
The Evil Dead.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.240
This is a pretty good list.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.240
Scream.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.240
Alien.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:32.240
The Thing.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:33.250
I approve of Google's list of favorite horror
movies.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.070
There's some good stuff on there.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.690
Tell me something creepy.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:41.510
Catnipsom says that a typical cat sleeps for
2/3 of it's life sleeping.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:46.510
That means by the time a cat is 9, it's only
been awake for 3 years.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.300
How is that creepy?

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.500
What?

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.630
What is this?

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:57.240
OK?

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.750
Oh, this is a V-Sauce video.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.370
I can't watch this.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.840
That's funny though.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.000
Tell me something scary.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.000
Did you hear--

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.840
No, you already told me this story!

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.470
Just tell me a story.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.990
It was a dark and stormy night.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.380
A scream rang out from the blackness.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:20.880
"Happy Birthday" shouted the Google Assistant
as the lights came on.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.290
OK...

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.290
It's not my birthday.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.520
I got mixed up.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:26.810
You should keep the cake though.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:28.310
Where's the cake?

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.840
I found a few locations.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:31.660
You need more stories, Google.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.150
This looks cool, mind tricks.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.820
Pick any number between 1 and 20.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.930
No, I hate these things.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.510
What are you gonna be for Halloween?

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.990
I still can't decide.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.830
Good thing I have a quiz that can help.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:43.830
What should I be for Halloween.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:44.830
Let's do that.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:46.830
Wow, I'm so glad you asked.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:50.290
I don't want to toot my own horn, but I'm
kind of an expert.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.790
Oh, hold on.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:52.790
Wait what?

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.290
Trick or treat!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:55.300
Nice costumes.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.370
Who's trick-or-treating at Google's house
in February?

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.010
OK, run along and have fun.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.010
Thank you!

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.199
I need to help someone now.

00:06:02.199 --> 00:06:03.240
Bye.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.290
OK.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:07.090
Let me access your costume interests with
a few questions.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.900
Do you regularly yell for other people to
bring you things?

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.900
I mean, does Uber Eats count?

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:14.960
That didn't seem like an answer.

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:16.430
I'm just gonna put no.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:17.430
Freaky answer!

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.430
Freaky!

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:21.730
Is it OK to read over an unsuspecting person's
shoulder?

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.160
Yeah why not?

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.160
Freak answer.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.160
Now try this one.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.160
Again.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.250
Do you change your toothbrush every few months?

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:28.250
No.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.830
Like I change the brush head, but I don't
change the toothbrush because it's an electric

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:31.830
toothbrush.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.340
Would you risk severe bruising just to make
a grumpy baby laugh?

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.300
Bruising on me or bruising on the baby?

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.180
I'm just gonna say Yes.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:40.990
That's a very telling answer.

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:41.990
One last question.

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:42.990
It's a big one.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:45.370
Pretend that you work for a really demanding
boss.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:47.490
And he asks you to get him a brain--

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.610
Oh that's so cool!

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.490
--it's for an important project--

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.050
I would totally be that boss.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.150
--before an electrical storm rolls into town.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:59.360
You heard there might be a damaged brain available
at the local brain depository.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:00.360
What do you do?

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:01.620
Get the brain.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.820
You gotta get the brain!

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:04.820
Awesome, thanks.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.400
Let me make a few quick calculations.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.400
Alright.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.660
Special delivery for Halloween.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.040
It's your head!

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:11.650
In a box.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.580
That's the costume!

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:14.760
Head in a box.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.760
That's the costume?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:17.830
Do you want to take the quiz again?

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.050
I don't want to take the quiz again.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:22.460
Ok, so the costume is basically that thing
from Se7en.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.460
OK.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.460
You know what.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.960
Self destruct.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:35.050
Self-destructing in 3, 2, 1.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:38.120
Actually I think I'll stick around.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.120
OK.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:40.120
Um.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.140
Oh here's a good one.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.170
Open the pod bay doors.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.360
I can't do that.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.240
But there's a spare key under the flowerpot
outside the pod bay airlock.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.759
You can let yourself in.

00:07:50.759 --> 00:07:51.759
Nice.

00:07:51.759 --> 00:07:57.070
Alright, well I think we got all of the creepy
stuff that we're gonna get out of Google Assistant.

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:59.860
I guess I just have one last thing to ask
it then.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:01.620
OK Google.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:06.930
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:10.729
notifications and I'll see you in the next
one.

00:08:10.729 --> 00:08:14.800
Assuming we both survive.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.470
When do you want to be reminded?

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.470
No.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.470
No...

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:33.969
That's not what-- I was doing the outro.

